# Slice 418 witness: the code of the unit's root runs over itself, so its `data` is the root Structure (docs/LMX_semantics.en.md
# #data-code-roles: a Structure launched alone is its own data; #ordinary-var: `data\x` is the path to the place x of the data of the current launch).
# `data\[0]raising := 1` writes the graph field of the root as `node\[0]raising` reads it in a fn (a write to a local of the root changes no graph
# field, #call-frame-20261115); `data\raising` reads the field by the same path.  Entry 7; 83 names a failing check.
int: raising 0
fn: peek () int
    return: node\[0]raising
data\[0]raising := 1
int: answer 83
if: peek() = 1 && data\raising = 1
    answer := 7
send: exit(exit_code: answer; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
